  "question": {
    "text": "Lying in the plane <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;is a line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;passing through <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and perpendicular to the line of intersection of planes <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> and <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the equation of <math><mi>L</mi></math> is",
